    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense is positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** and **Kyle Tucker**. **Gunnar Henderson** earns the day's highest efficiency score (83.29) due to a favorable matchup against Roki Sasaki; his projection is bolstered by an elite platoon advantage, wind conditions favoring power, and a high-probability SB environment against the pitcher's slow delivery. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** (81.06) is a prime start against Trey Gibson. Given the scarcity of speed, **Cole Carrigg** (65.69) is another vital piece; he benefits from a park factor boost of +14% and switch-hitting versatility, making him a strong anchor alongside **Andy Pages** (75.64), who draws the same favorable matchup against Gibson.\n\nStrategic decisions at the margins reflect our focus on optimizing platoon edges and order placement. **Nolan Schanuel** (65.98) and **Josh Jung** (65.53) provide steady production, with both hitters benefiting from favorable SP skill metrics for their respective matchups. The tightest call on the bench involved **Coby Mayo** (55.69); while he presents a legitimate threat against Roki Sasaki, the optimizer favored **Jacob Wilson** (58.23) due to a stronger projected lineup position and a significant park factor advantage that outweighed the raw output potential of **Coby Mayo**. We are monitoring the pending lineup statuses for **Liam Hicks**, **Drake Baldwin**, and **Jackson Merrill**, as adjustments to their batting order could shift their efficiency scores significantly before first pitch.\n\nOwners should remain cautious regarding **Jackson Merrill** (52.34), who faces the elite Jacob deGrom. While his dynamic platoon advantage keeps him in the starting XI, his score is depressed by the pitcher's efficiency at holding runners, limiting his utility in the SB category. Likewise, **Wade Meckler** (44.15) remains a marginal play; despite favorable park dynamics, his low-leadoff spot and a poor L/L platoon matchup make him the most vulnerable member of the active roster today. All starters should be considered locked unless late-breaking lineup data forces a pivot to the bench.",
